<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/">
    <!--
        The escort-quest confirm (decision 1733): one StaticPopup entry on our shared engine
        (UiPanels.xml) plus its event driver. The patch-chain FrameXML is the SPECIFICATION —
        StaticPopup.lua l.727-737 (the QUEST_ACCEPT entry) and UIParent.lua l.93 + l.353-356 (the
        registration and the one-line arm) — and it fixes the dialog key, the field names and the
        one verb by name, so those are reproduced exactly.

        WHY THIS IS ITS OWN FILE, next to QuestFrame.xml and QuestLogFrame.xml rather than inside
        either. It belongs to neither window. The confirm has no window at all — it is raised by
        `crate::ui_quest_share` off `SMSG_QUEST_CONFIRM_ACCEPT`, exactly as DuelFrame.xml's two
        dialogs are raised off the duel packets, and answering it sends a packet neither quest
        window knows about. Putting it in QuestFrame.xml would say the questgiver panel owns it
        (it does not — no panel is open when this arrives) and putting it in QuestLogFrame.xml
        would say the log window does (it does not either: the log is closed for most players when
        a party member starts an escort).

        WHAT RAISES IT. `QUEST_FLAGS_PARTY_ACCEPT` (0x2) quests — escorts. When a party member
        accepts one, the server asks every other eligible member whether they want it too
        (vmangos `QuestHandler.cpp:172-193`). That is a DIFFERENT flow from the quest-log's *Share
        Quest* button, which needs no dialog at all: a pushed quest arrives on the ordinary
        questgiver detail panel (QuestFrame.xml) with the sharer's player guid where an NPC's
        would be, and Accept/Decline there are the whole answer.

        THE ONE ASYMMETRY, and it is the reference's, not ours: Yes calls ConfirmAcceptQuest() and
        sends `CMSG_QUEST_CONFIRM_ACCEPT`; **No sends nothing at all**. There is no OnCancel below
        because there is no packet for one — the server's pending-share latch is simply cleared by
        the next thing that touches it. The same is true of ESC (hideOnEscape).
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- The shipped enUS GlobalStrings.lua values, quoted as data (l.3227, and the YES/NO pair).
        -- First %s is the party member's name, second is the quest title — the argument order
        -- QUEST_ACCEPT_CONFIRM fires with.
        local QUEST_ACCEPT = "%s is starting %s\nWould you like to as well?"

        StaticPopupDialogs["QUEST_ACCEPT"] = {
            text = QUEST_ACCEPT,
            button1 = "Yes",  -- YES
            button2 = "No",   -- NO
            OnAccept = function()
                ConfirmAcceptQuest()
            end,
            timeout = 0,
            exclusive = 1,
            hideOnEscape = 1,
        }

        -- spec: UIParent.lua l.353-356 — one arm, both args straight through.
        function BenillaQuestShareDriver_OnEvent()
            if event == "QUEST_ACCEPT_CONFIRM" then
                StaticPopup_Show("QUEST_ACCEPT", arg1, arg2)
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>

    <Frame name="BenillaQuestShareDriver" hidden="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="1" y="1"/></Size>
        <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>self:RegisterEvent("QUEST_ACCEPT_CONFIRM")</OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>BenillaQuestShareDriver_OnEvent()</OnEvent>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>
</Ui>
